      "Bash(gh pr create --title \"fix\\(INFRA-22\\): make database safety checks conditional\" --body \"$\\(cat <<''EOF''\n## Summary\n\n- Makes database safety checks work correctly with required status checks in GitHub rulesets\n- Adds `check-paths` job using `dorny/paths-filter` to detect database file changes\n- All other jobs skip gracefully when no database files are changed\n- Skipped jobs report as \"Success\", allowing non-database PRs to merge\n\n## Problem\n\nWhen database safety checks \\(`migration-validation`, `migration-testing`, `security-analysis`\\) are required in GitHub rulesets, PRs that don''t touch database files get stuck forever waiting for status checks that will never run.\n\n## Solution\n\nBased on [GitHub Actions Required Checks for Conditional Jobs]\\(https://devopsdirective.com/posts/2025/08/github-actions-required-checks-for-conditional-jobs/\\):\n\n1. Remove path filtering from `pull_request` trigger \\(workflow now runs on all PRs\\)\n2. Add `check-paths` job that determines if database files changed\n3. All other jobs depend on `check-paths` output and skip if no database files changed\n4. Skipped jobs report \"Success\" status, satisfying required checks\n\n## Linear Issue\n\nhttps://linear.app/convergent-app/issue/INFRA-22\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [ ] This PR itself tests the fix - it doesn''t touch database files\n- [ ] Verify `check-paths` job runs and reports no database changes\n- [ ] Verify other jobs skip and report Success\n- [ ] Verify PR can be merged\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code]\\(https://claude.com/claude-code\\)\nEOF\n\\)\")",
